1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,060
you

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,060
you

3
00:00:38,060 --> 00:00:45,420
Krishnamurti in dialogue with Dr. Alan W. Anderson. J. Krishnamurti was born in

4
00:00:45,420 --> 00:00:50,640
South India and educated in England. For the past 40 years he has been speaking

5
00:00:50,640 --> 00:00:55,640
in the United States, Europe, India, Australia, and other parts of the world.

6
00:00:55,640 --> 00:01:00,400
From the outset of his life's work he repudiated all connections with

7
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:05,360
organized religions and ideologies and said that his only concern was to set

8
00:01:05,360 --> 00:01:11,600
men absolutely unconditionally free. He is the author of many books, among them

9
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:17,240
The Awakening of Intelligence, The Urgency of Change, Freedom from the Known, and

10
00:01:17,240 --> 00:01:23,840
The Flight of the Eagle. This is one of a series of dialogues between Krishnamurti

11
00:01:23,840 --> 00:01:28,040
and Dr. Alan W. Anderson who is professor of religious studies at San

12
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:32,400
Diego State University where he teaches Indian and Chinese scriptures and the

13
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:38,480
oracular tradition. Dr. Anderson, a published poet, received his degree from

14
00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:43,120
Columbia University and the Union Theological Seminary. He has been honored

15
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:51,800
with a Distinguished Teaching Award from the California State Universities. Mr.

16
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:58,680
Krishnamurti, in our series of conversations we've reached, it seems to

17
00:01:58,680 --> 00:02:09,400
me, an especially critical place. In our last discussion together we touched on

18
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:17,000
the question of authority, not only in relation to what is out there that we

19
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:24,360
project and what is out there that faces us, literally, but also the question at

20
00:02:24,360 --> 00:02:33,120
the deeper level of my relationship within and the point where in the

21
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:42,280
inquiry, in going deeply into myself, in self-examination, there is a point of

22
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:52,600
boggling, one boggles, one is hesitant and trembles. It is a real fear and

23
00:02:52,600 --> 00:03:01,240
trembling that occurs at the brink of that inquiry. And I think you were at the

24
00:03:01,240 --> 00:03:09,600
conclusion of our former conversation, moving toward a discussion of that in

25
00:03:09,600 --> 00:03:14,760
terms of its role in the religious life.

26
00:03:14,760 --> 00:03:17,760
That's right.

27
00:03:22,400 --> 00:03:30,880
Sir, why do we hesitate? That's what comes to what you're saying. Why do we

28
00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:35,240
not take the plunge? That's what you're asking.

29
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:36,840
That's what I'm asking, yes.

30
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:44,080
Why is this always coming to the brink and withdrawing, running away?

31
00:03:46,280 --> 00:03:53,400
Why don't we see the thing as is and act?

32
00:03:54,400 --> 00:04:08,760
Is it, sir, part of our education that has cultivated function, enormous function?

33
00:04:08,760 --> 00:04:16,600
We give tremendous importance to function, as an engineer, as a professor, as a

34
00:04:16,840 --> 00:04:25,160
doctor and so on and so on, functioning in a particular technique. And we have never

35
00:04:25,160 --> 00:04:32,760
cultivated or encouraged or enquired into what is intelligence. Where there is

36
00:04:32,760 --> 00:04:39,720
intelligence there won't be this hesitation, there is action. I mean, when

37
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:53,200
one is very sensitive, you act. That sensitivity is intelligence. Now, in

38
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:58,800
education, as I have observed it both here and in India and other parts of the

39
00:04:58,800 --> 00:05:07,360
world, education is merely the training in the mind to function to the

40
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:19,320
dictates of society. So many engineers are wanted, so many doctors are wanted. If you

41
00:05:19,320 --> 00:05:24,520
get into a profession where there are few, you might make more money.

42
00:05:24,520 --> 00:05:26,560
A. You have to watch out for the glut.

43
00:05:26,560 --> 00:05:31,960
K. Glut. Don't become a two-scientific, or enough scientific, or whatever it is.

44
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:33,280
A. Oh dear, yes.

45
00:05:33,280 --> 00:05:41,040
K. So we are encouraged and trained to function in the field of activity as functions,

46
00:05:41,040 --> 00:05:52,520
careers. Now, we hesitate to enter or plunge into something that demands all

47
00:05:52,520 --> 00:06:02,840
your attention, not fragmentarily, all your attention, because we don't know

48
00:06:02,840 --> 00:06:10,640
what the measure is. We know how to measure function. Here we have no measure.

49
00:06:10,640 --> 00:06:18,680
Therefore I depend. Therefore I won't reason here, because I don't know how to

50
00:06:18,800 --> 00:06:30,440
reason. I don't say to a man who says, I know. I say, what do you know? You only know

51
00:06:30,440 --> 00:06:42,360
something that is gone, finished, dead. You can't say, I know something that is living.

52
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:55,920
And so gradually, as I see it, the mind becomes dull, restless, its curiosity is only in the

53
00:06:55,920 --> 00:07:09,760
direction of functioning, and it has no capacity to enquire. To enquire you must have freedom

54
00:07:09,760 --> 00:07:17,080
first. I can't enquire otherwise. If I come to enquire to something which I have to enquire

55
00:07:17,080 --> 00:07:24,360
about, if I have prejudices, I can't enquire. If I have conclusions about that, I can't enquire.

56
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:37,600
Therefore there must be freedom to enquire. And that is denied, because society and culture

57
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:45,880
have laid tremendous importance on function. And function has its own status.

58
00:07:45,880 --> 00:07:50,600
A. Oh yes, yes. It's exalted ultimately into process.

59
00:07:50,600 --> 00:07:59,880
K. Yes, into a status. So status matters much more than function. And so I live in that

60
00:07:59,880 --> 00:08:07,360
field, live in that structure, and therefore I want to enquire into religion. What is religion,

61
00:08:07,360 --> 00:08:16,160
what is God, what is immortality, what is beauty? I can't do it. I depend on an authority.

62
00:08:16,160 --> 00:08:37,720
And so I have no basis for reasoning. You follow, sir? In this vast field of religion. So it is partly

63
00:08:38,280 --> 00:08:51,040
fault of our education, partly our incapacity to look at anything objectively. Our incapacity

64
00:08:51,040 --> 00:08:57,740
to look at a tree without all the rigmarole, knowledge, screen, blocks, that prevents me

65
00:08:57,740 --> 00:09:06,420
from looking at the tree. I never look at my wife, if I have a wife, or a girl, whatever,

66
00:09:06,420 --> 00:09:16,780
I never look. I look at her or him through the image about him or her. So the image is

67
00:09:16,780 --> 00:09:30,160
a dead, dead thing. So I never look at a living thing. I never look at nature with all the

68
00:09:30,160 --> 00:09:36,760
marvel of it, the beauty of it, the shape, the loveliness of it, but I am always translating

69
00:09:36,760 --> 00:09:48,120
it, trying to paint it, write about it, or enjoy it. You follow? So from that arises

70
00:09:48,120 --> 00:10:03,660
the question, why do human beings accept authority, obey? Is it because they have been trained

71
00:10:03,660 --> 00:10:12,000
in the field of function where you must obey, to learn? You follow? You can't just...

72
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:17,400
A. No, it has its own laws, built in. K. No, it has its own disciplines, it has its own

73
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:25,360
laws, its own ways. Because I have been trained that way, I bring that over here into the

74
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:32,660
field of religion, into the field of something that demands freedom, freedom not at the end,

75
00:10:32,660 --> 00:10:41,780
right from the beginning. Mind must be free from authority from the beginning. If I want

76
00:10:41,780 --> 00:10:50,160
to find out what is God, not, I believe in God, that's no meaning. If there is God, if

77
00:10:50,160 --> 00:10:59,160
there is no God, I really want to find out. I am terribly serious. And if I am really

78
00:10:59,160 --> 00:11:07,100
serious, I am really concerned to the understanding, learning about God, if there is God, I must

79
00:11:07,100 --> 00:11:15,140
push aside completely all the beliefs, all the structure, all the churches, all the priests,

80
00:11:15,140 --> 00:11:23,180
all the books, all the things that thought has put together about religion. You follow?

81
00:11:23,180 --> 00:11:31,840
A. Yes, I do. I have been thinking very hard about your word intelligence and the word truth in

82
00:11:31,840 --> 00:11:39,920
relation to what you have been saying, and the passage from the Gospel came to my mind, which

83
00:11:39,920 --> 00:11:45,720
would end up, I think, with a very different exegesis in terms of what you have been saying.

84
00:11:45,720 --> 00:11:53,460
If one applied what you've been pointing to, to this text, when he the Spirit of Truth has come,

85
00:11:53,460 --> 00:12:04,220
he will guide you into all truth, and the truth shall make you free. The truth is called a spirit

86
00:12:04,220 --> 00:12:15,380
here, and in the very same St. John's Gospel, God is also called Spirit, a radical act, not this

87
00:12:15,380 --> 00:12:21,820
spirit over there, out there somewhere, that I have projected. If one takes seriously,

88
00:12:21,820 --> 00:12:25,540
the terrible thing is that it hasn't been taken seriously.

89
00:12:25,540 --> 00:12:30,180
K. Because we are not allowed to be serious, sir.

90
00:12:30,180 --> 00:12:34,380
A. We can't even be serious about the thing that is claimed we must be the most serious about.

91
00:12:34,380 --> 00:12:35,740
K. That's just it.

92
00:12:35,740 --> 00:12:36,820
A. Yes, I know.

93
00:12:37,820 --> 00:12:46,860
K. We are not serious about our children. We don't feel responsible for them. Right through life,

94
00:12:46,860 --> 00:12:52,540
only when they are till they are four, five, six, we are responsible, you know. After that they can

95
00:12:53,540 --> 00:13:07,580
do what they want. So, freedom and authority cannot possibly exist together. Freedom and

96
00:13:07,580 --> 00:13:18,820
intelligence go together. And intelligence has its own innate, natural, easy discipline,

97
00:13:18,820 --> 00:13:29,060
in the sense of not suppression, control, imitation, all that, but discipline, which is the act of

98
00:13:29,060 --> 00:13:30,900
learning all the time.

99
00:13:30,900 --> 00:13:34,260
A. In attention.

100
00:13:34,260 --> 00:13:35,140
K. Yes, in attention.

101
00:13:35,140 --> 00:13:43,180
A. In attention. This intelligence that you speak of is associated with splendour, isn't it?

102
00:13:44,180 --> 00:13:51,340
It's advent is immediate, not gradual.

103
00:13:51,340 --> 00:13:54,620
K. No, of course, sir. The perception is intelligence.

104
00:13:54,620 --> 00:13:56,180
A. The perception is intelligence.

105
00:13:56,180 --> 00:13:57,180
K. And therefore acting.

106
00:13:57,180 --> 00:13:57,980
A. And the perception is the act.

107
00:13:57,980 --> 00:13:59,060
K. Of course.

108
00:13:59,060 --> 00:14:05,180
A. So the act, intelligence, beauty, love, truth, freedom...

109
00:14:05,180 --> 00:14:07,620
K. And death, all the one...

110
00:14:07,620 --> 00:14:17,940
A. ...they form a complete, total, integral movement in act.

111
00:14:17,940 --> 00:14:26,140
That in itself, looked at positively, is even, once it's translated into a concept...

112
00:14:26,140 --> 00:14:27,540
K. Oh, then it's no longer that.

113
00:14:27,540 --> 00:14:31,740
A. ...becomes in itself an occasion for terror again.

114
00:14:31,740 --> 00:14:32,180
K. Of course.

115
00:14:32,180 --> 00:14:35,380
A. Because it seems that it runs away too fast from you.

116
00:14:35,380 --> 00:14:35,700
K. Yes.

117
00:14:35,700 --> 00:14:41,020
A. As soon as you... Yes, I see. Isn't that marvellous?

118
00:14:41,020 --> 00:14:47,860
It's as though these that you've mentioned, beauty, intelligence, love, freedom...

119
00:14:47,860 --> 00:14:49,060
K. And death.

120
00:14:49,060 --> 00:14:55,180
A. ...have, so to speak, secured themselves against all tomfoolery.

121
00:14:55,180 --> 00:14:57,940
K. Yes, sir. Tomfoolery, quite right.

122
00:14:57,940 --> 00:15:02,900
A. They have just... they are so radically pure.

123
00:15:02,900 --> 00:15:04,500
They're any foolery.

124
00:15:04,500 --> 00:15:11,980
So, sir, that means, can the mind put aside totally

125
00:15:11,980 --> 00:15:19,100
all the structure of thought with regard to religion?

126
00:15:21,180 --> 00:15:29,700
It can't put away the function of thought in the field of knowledge.

127
00:15:29,700 --> 00:15:32,420
That's what I've understood, that's very clear.

128
00:15:32,420 --> 00:15:37,180
But here there is something I don't know, we don't know.

129
00:15:37,180 --> 00:15:42,300
You follow, sir? We pretend we know.

130
00:15:42,300 --> 00:15:47,220
When the man says, Jesus is the saviour, or whatever,

131
00:15:47,220 --> 00:15:51,420
it is a pretension.

132
00:15:51,420 --> 00:15:55,540
It is saying, I know, and you don't know.

133
00:15:55,540 --> 00:15:57,860
What do you know in the name of heaven?

134
00:15:57,860 --> 00:16:01,660
You know nothing. You just repeat.

135
00:16:01,660 --> 00:16:05,580
What you have learnt from somebody else.

136
00:16:05,580 --> 00:16:11,300
So can the mind, in the field of religion,

137
00:16:11,300 --> 00:16:12,660
which is the most...

138
00:16:12,660 --> 00:16:17,020
because religion is, as we said at the beginning,

139
00:16:17,020 --> 00:16:22,620
the gathering of all energy in that quality of attention.

140
00:16:22,620 --> 00:16:29,580
And it is that quality of attention that regenerates man,

141
00:16:29,580 --> 00:16:34,340
that brings about real transformation in man

142
00:16:34,340 --> 00:16:37,380
with regard to his conduct, his behaviour,

143
00:16:37,380 --> 00:16:43,740
his whole way of relationship, religion, is that factor.

144
00:16:43,740 --> 00:16:48,420
Not all this foolery that's going on.

145
00:16:48,420 --> 00:16:53,660
Now, to enquire,

146
00:16:54,220 --> 00:17:00,260
the mind must put aside all the structure of thought

147
00:17:00,260 --> 00:17:04,500
built around that word.

148
00:17:05,300 --> 00:17:09,900
You follow, sir? Can one do it?

149
00:17:09,900 --> 00:17:14,300
If not, we are pretending, talking about God, no God, yes God,

150
00:17:14,300 --> 00:17:19,660
you follow, all that nonsense that is going on.

151
00:17:20,660 --> 00:17:23,420
So, that's the first question.

152
00:17:23,420 --> 00:17:29,900
Can the mind be free of the authority of another,

153
00:17:29,900 --> 00:17:34,340
however great, however sublime, however divine, or no divine?

154
00:17:34,340 --> 00:17:35,820
You follow?

155
00:17:35,820 --> 00:17:39,940
A. And because an act is required in order to answer this question...

156
00:17:39,940 --> 00:17:42,140
K. Absolutely.

157
00:17:42,140 --> 00:17:45,900
A. ...the individual must do this on his own.

158
00:17:45,900 --> 00:17:50,980
Otherwise he merely lives in a routine of function,

159
00:17:50,980 --> 00:17:53,340
which he has, which he is still doing,

160
00:17:53,340 --> 00:17:58,460
and therefore he escapes into all these circuses,

161
00:17:58,460 --> 00:18:01,580
which he calls religion.

162
00:18:01,580 --> 00:18:04,860
A. This came home to me with great dramatic force

163
00:18:04,860 --> 00:18:06,740
yesterday in class.

164
00:18:06,740 --> 00:18:11,180
On the one hand we have textbooks,

165
00:18:11,180 --> 00:18:14,020
textbooks which have survived the centuries

166
00:18:14,020 --> 00:18:19,020
because of their classical value in that sense,

167
00:18:21,340 --> 00:18:29,980
and the usual way in which this material is taught

168
00:18:29,980 --> 00:18:32,380
is that one learns, let us say,

169
00:18:32,380 --> 00:18:35,260
something about the Chinese vision of life.

170
00:18:35,260 --> 00:18:38,620
Then we have the Hindu vision of life,

171
00:18:38,620 --> 00:18:42,820
and so we accumulate over a long period of time through school,

172
00:18:42,820 --> 00:18:44,580
clear through graduate school,

173
00:18:44,580 --> 00:18:48,980
if you hang in there long enough, you can stand it,

174
00:18:48,980 --> 00:18:51,740
you come into possession of...

175
00:18:51,740 --> 00:18:54,420
K. What other people have said.

176
00:18:54,420 --> 00:18:56,340
But you know nothing about it.

177
00:18:56,340 --> 00:18:57,780
A. Exactly.

178
00:18:57,780 --> 00:19:02,060
You acquire certain skills in the order of function,

179
00:19:02,060 --> 00:19:04,020
as you have mentioned.

180
00:19:04,020 --> 00:19:05,580
Now the teacher has a problem.

181
00:19:05,580 --> 00:19:11,060
I am thinking of these schools that you have referred to in India,

182
00:19:11,060 --> 00:19:14,660
and the one that will be in Ojai.

183
00:19:14,660 --> 00:19:17,100
There is a body of material here.

184
00:19:17,100 --> 00:19:20,220
Clearly the teacher must be in possession of knowledge

185
00:19:20,220 --> 00:19:22,260
in the order of functional operation,

186
00:19:22,260 --> 00:19:23,980
procedural techniques and so forth.

187
00:19:23,980 --> 00:19:26,660
He simply has to know.

188
00:19:26,660 --> 00:19:29,700
The child is going to read books

189
00:19:29,700 --> 00:19:31,420
in these schools that you have mentioned.

190
00:19:31,420 --> 00:19:33,340
K. Oh, they do. A. They read books.

191
00:19:33,340 --> 00:19:37,380
Books, all of them haven't been written necessarily by somebody

192
00:19:37,420 --> 00:19:41,340
who is undertaking to do the thing that goes on

193
00:19:41,340 --> 00:19:44,980
between the students and the teachers in these schools.

194
00:19:44,980 --> 00:19:50,380
Now the teacher must handle this written material in books,

195
00:19:50,380 --> 00:19:55,820
in a way to indicate to the child,

196
00:19:55,820 --> 00:19:58,540
the young student, the older student,

197
00:19:58,540 --> 00:20:00,940
that it is possible to read this material

198
00:20:00,940 --> 00:20:03,860
without being self-divided in doing it.

199
00:20:03,860 --> 00:20:12,220
And also, what would you do if there was no book?

200
00:20:14,740 --> 00:20:16,620
A. You would be in the same position.

201
00:20:16,620 --> 00:20:20,900
K. Now, if there was no book,

202
00:20:20,900 --> 00:20:25,420
nobody says tradition,

203
00:20:25,420 --> 00:20:29,380
you had to find out for yourself.

204
00:20:29,380 --> 00:20:32,340
A. But that's what we are asking him to do with his book,

205
00:20:32,340 --> 00:20:34,060
aren't we? K. Are we?

206
00:20:34,060 --> 00:20:39,820
A. No, not in general, but in this new approach.

207
00:20:39,820 --> 00:20:42,220
In the new approach we must somehow...

208
00:20:42,220 --> 00:20:44,020
K. ...bring the book and the other.

209
00:20:44,020 --> 00:20:45,940
A. Bring the book and the other together.

210
00:20:45,940 --> 00:20:48,180
K. And the freedom. Book and freedom.

211
00:20:48,180 --> 00:20:53,780
A. Yes. This is what hit me with such shock yesterday in class.

212
00:20:53,780 --> 00:20:58,180
And I immediately felt radically responsible for doing this,

213
00:20:58,180 --> 00:21:00,340
insofar as I could.

214
00:21:00,340 --> 00:21:04,020
And I was surprised to see that,

215
00:21:04,020 --> 00:21:10,420
though the students were extremely hesitant,

216
00:21:10,420 --> 00:21:18,620
there was a lot of anxiety there, real fear and trembling.

217
00:21:18,620 --> 00:21:25,100
What of health they possessed did assert itself.

218
00:21:25,100 --> 00:21:35,380
And there was a tremendous interest in the possibility.

219
00:21:35,380 --> 00:21:38,740
But then there was the hesitation

220
00:21:38,740 --> 00:21:42,860
that somehow wasn't passed.

221
00:21:42,860 --> 00:21:45,660
The hesitation is there.

222
00:21:45,660 --> 00:21:48,180
I have this feeling that this has happened

223
00:21:48,180 --> 00:21:54,540
through the centuries with persons

224
00:21:54,540 --> 00:21:57,660
who have seriously studied scripture,

225
00:21:57,660 --> 00:22:00,580
since we were talking about religion.

226
00:22:00,580 --> 00:22:03,340
Sometimes you can detect it in their very commentaries,

227
00:22:03,340 --> 00:22:04,540
in their very writing.

228
00:22:04,540 --> 00:22:07,460
They come right up to it. K. And miss it.

229
00:22:07,460 --> 00:22:11,780
A. And then they can't push it over.

230
00:22:11,780 --> 00:22:16,140
They can't go beyond the point.

231
00:22:16,140 --> 00:22:21,860
K. That's, sir, it has been my fortune or misfortune

232
00:22:21,860 --> 00:22:25,380
to talk a great deal.

233
00:22:25,380 --> 00:22:29,460
Everybody comes to that point

234
00:22:29,460 --> 00:22:31,140
and says, please, what am I to do?

235
00:22:31,140 --> 00:22:36,980
I have reached that point, I can't go beyond.

236
00:22:36,980 --> 00:22:41,580
Sir, look at it this way, if I may suggest.

237
00:22:41,580 --> 00:22:46,980
If I had a class, I wouldn't talk about the book first.

238
00:22:46,980 --> 00:22:51,020
I'd say, freedom.

239
00:22:51,020 --> 00:22:54,540
You are second-hand people.

240
00:22:54,540 --> 00:22:58,140
Don't pretend you are not.

241
00:22:58,140 --> 00:23:03,420
You are second-hand, sloppy, shoddy people.

242
00:23:03,420 --> 00:23:08,820
And you are trying to find something that is original.

243
00:23:08,820 --> 00:23:11,820
The reality is original.

244
00:23:11,820 --> 00:23:17,220
It's not coloured by all the priests in the world.

245
00:23:17,220 --> 00:23:19,340
It's original.

246
00:23:19,340 --> 00:23:22,180
Therefore you must have an original mind,

247
00:23:22,180 --> 00:23:25,660
which means a free mind.

248
00:23:25,660 --> 00:23:28,740
Not an original painting, a new picture, a new this,

249
00:23:28,740 --> 00:23:35,260
that's all tommyrot, but a free mind.

250
00:23:35,260 --> 00:23:40,460
A free mind that can function in the field of knowledge,

251
00:23:40,460 --> 00:23:46,340
and a free mind that can look, observe, learn.

252
00:23:46,340 --> 00:23:50,540
Now, how do you help another,

253
00:23:50,540 --> 00:23:54,580
or is it not possible to be free?

254
00:23:54,580 --> 00:23:57,420
You understand?

255
00:23:57,420 --> 00:24:02,940
Look, I never belong to anything.

256
00:24:02,940 --> 00:24:08,140
I am no church, I have no belief, all that.

257
00:24:10,740 --> 00:24:13,340
A man who really wants to find out

258
00:24:13,340 --> 00:24:17,340
if there is eternal, the nameless,

259
00:24:17,340 --> 00:24:20,740
something beyond all thought,

260
00:24:20,740 --> 00:24:27,980
he must naturally set aside everything built on thought.

261
00:24:27,980 --> 00:24:32,260
The saviour, the masters, the gurus, the knowledge,

262
00:24:32,260 --> 00:24:35,140
all that must...

263
00:24:36,620 --> 00:24:39,900
Are there people to do that?

264
00:24:39,900 --> 00:24:41,100
You follow?

265
00:24:41,100 --> 00:24:45,220
Will anybody undertake that journey?

266
00:24:45,220 --> 00:24:48,020
Or you say, well, you tell me all about it, old boy,

267
00:24:48,020 --> 00:24:52,340
I'll sit comfortably and then you tell me.

268
00:24:52,340 --> 00:24:54,740
A. Yes, yes, that's what goes on.

269
00:24:54,740 --> 00:24:57,660
K. I say, I won't describe that,

270
00:24:57,660 --> 00:25:00,940
I won't tell you a thing about it.

271
00:25:00,940 --> 00:25:05,020
To put it into words is to destroy it.

272
00:25:06,020 --> 00:25:11,020
So, let us see if you cannot be free.

273
00:25:11,020 --> 00:25:14,980
What are you frightened about?

274
00:25:14,980 --> 00:25:18,340
Frightened of authority, frightened of going wrong,

275
00:25:18,340 --> 00:25:23,700
but you are completely wrong the way you live,

276
00:25:23,700 --> 00:25:26,820
completely stupid the way you are carrying on.

277
00:25:26,820 --> 00:25:30,860
It has no meaning.

278
00:25:30,860 --> 00:25:33,980
Keep... You follow, sir?

279
00:25:33,980 --> 00:25:41,380
Deny the spiritual authority of every kind.

280
00:25:42,860 --> 00:25:45,260
Because what are you frightened of?

281
00:25:45,260 --> 00:25:48,020
Going wrong spiritually?

282
00:25:48,020 --> 00:25:50,500
They are wrong, not you are wrong,

283
00:25:50,500 --> 00:25:52,780
because you are just learning.

284
00:25:52,780 --> 00:25:59,740
They are the established in unrighteousness.

285
00:25:59,740 --> 00:26:05,420
Now, that is beautiful.

286
00:26:05,420 --> 00:26:11,020
And so why do you follow them? Why do you accept them?

287
00:26:11,020 --> 00:26:12,860
They are degenerate.

288
00:26:12,860 --> 00:26:16,460
And can you be free from all that,

289
00:26:16,460 --> 00:26:20,220
so that your mind, through meditation,

290
00:26:20,220 --> 00:26:23,260
which we will discuss perhaps another time,

291
00:26:23,260 --> 00:26:25,780
what it means to be free,

292
00:26:25,780 --> 00:26:30,100
what it means to wipe away all the things

293
00:26:30,100 --> 00:26:33,100
that people have put on you.

294
00:26:33,100 --> 00:26:37,740
You understand? So that you are innocent,

295
00:26:37,740 --> 00:26:40,540
your mind is never hurt,

296
00:26:40,540 --> 00:26:44,020
is incapable of being hurt.

297
00:26:44,020 --> 00:26:47,820
That is what innocence means.

298
00:26:47,820 --> 00:26:53,260
And from that, enquire, let's take a journey from there.

299
00:26:53,260 --> 00:26:55,380
You follow, sir?

300
00:26:55,380 --> 00:27:00,540
From this sense of negation of everything

301
00:27:00,540 --> 00:27:02,900
that thought has put together,

302
00:27:02,900 --> 00:27:08,900
because thought is time, thought is matter.

303
00:27:08,900 --> 00:27:14,180
And if you are living in the field of thought,

304
00:27:14,180 --> 00:27:19,460
there will be never freedom.

305
00:27:19,460 --> 00:27:23,300
You are living in the past.

306
00:27:23,300 --> 00:27:25,220
You may think you are living in the present,

307
00:27:25,220 --> 00:27:26,980
but actually you are living in the past

308
00:27:26,980 --> 00:27:28,740
when thought is in operation,

309
00:27:28,740 --> 00:27:31,540
because thought is a response of memory,

310
00:27:31,540 --> 00:27:34,900
knowledge, experience, stored up in the brain.

311
00:27:34,900 --> 00:27:40,780
And that knowledge, experience,

312
00:27:40,780 --> 00:27:43,700
is the expression of thought.

313
00:27:43,700 --> 00:27:48,940
Unless you understand that and know the limitation of thought,

314
00:27:48,940 --> 00:27:55,020
you can't enter into the field of that which you call religion.

315
00:27:55,020 --> 00:27:56,020
You follow, sir?

316
00:27:56,020 --> 00:28:02,540
Unless this is told, repeated, shown to them,

317
00:28:02,540 --> 00:28:05,540
you can talk endlessly about books.

318
00:28:05,540 --> 00:28:07,340
This comes first.

319
00:28:07,340 --> 00:28:11,780
Then you can read the books.

320
00:28:11,780 --> 00:28:12,780
A. Yes.

321
00:28:12,780 --> 00:28:15,980
K. Sir, they never read a book.

322
00:28:15,980 --> 00:28:20,860
You listen, watch, look, observe, fasted,

323
00:28:20,860 --> 00:28:26,580
say, all that's rubbish, and threw it out.

324
00:28:26,580 --> 00:28:30,540
A. I just noticed something that you said.

325
00:28:30,540 --> 00:28:35,260
One must keep on repeating this, again...

326
00:28:35,260 --> 00:28:40,460
K. In different ways. A. ...in different ways, and again.

327
00:28:40,460 --> 00:28:47,260
I am speaking now about teaching.

328
00:28:47,260 --> 00:28:51,660
This point of hesitation

329
00:28:51,660 --> 00:28:59,220
is the point where something will or will not get born.

330
00:28:59,220 --> 00:29:03,140
That beautiful expression in earlier conversation of ours

331
00:29:03,140 --> 00:29:06,900
that you used, incarnate now.

332
00:29:06,900 --> 00:29:10,020
So we are on the brink,

333
00:29:10,020 --> 00:29:13,820
where, in the words of Ortega I mentioned earlier,

334
00:29:13,820 --> 00:29:17,180
we are rocking back and forth on the brink of a new event,

335
00:29:17,180 --> 00:29:20,220
and we are not over the line.

336
00:29:20,220 --> 00:29:24,460
There is nothing that any of us can do at that point

337
00:29:24,460 --> 00:29:30,300
with respect to the terror of the one who hears this,

338
00:29:30,300 --> 00:29:31,900
including my own.

339
00:29:31,900 --> 00:29:38,820
I am not dividing myself from this doing together with the student,

340
00:29:38,820 --> 00:29:43,300
since I am a student in this activity.

341
00:29:43,300 --> 00:29:47,740
So here we are, student among students,

342
00:29:47,740 --> 00:29:58,060
and there is this boggling, this fear and trembling,

343
00:29:58,060 --> 00:30:04,780
and nothing can be done other than simply encourage.

344
00:30:04,780 --> 00:30:08,540
K. And tell them, wait, stay there.

345
00:30:08,540 --> 00:30:10,740
A. Hold. K. Hold.

346
00:30:10,740 --> 00:30:15,700
Doesn't matter if you wobble, but keep on wobbling.

347
00:30:15,700 --> 00:30:20,660
A. Don't bolt. K. Don't run away.

348
00:30:21,540 --> 00:30:26,900
A. And so this is said in different ways over and over again.

349
00:30:26,900 --> 00:30:28,620
Now I understand what you meant by saying,

350
00:30:28,620 --> 00:30:34,180
now let's start the class ten minutes with this.

351
00:30:34,180 --> 00:30:37,140
We don't open the book.

352
00:30:37,140 --> 00:30:39,500
We start with this.

353
00:30:39,500 --> 00:30:41,220
And then when the book is opened,

354
00:30:41,220 --> 00:30:45,780
perhaps the word for a change will disclose itself.

355
00:30:45,780 --> 00:30:49,220
Because intelligence has broken up,

356
00:30:49,220 --> 00:30:51,900
and behold, it's all splendid.

357
00:30:51,900 --> 00:30:55,380
Yes, yes, please, I didn't mean to interrupt you.

358
00:30:55,380 --> 00:30:57,420
I just wanted to make sure that I have...

359
00:30:57,420 --> 00:31:00,820
it's terribly important that I understand this.

360
00:31:00,820 --> 00:31:08,900
You see, sir, students rush from one class to the other,

361
00:31:08,900 --> 00:31:11,340
because the period is short, run.

362
00:31:11,340 --> 00:31:13,860
From mathematics, geography,

363
00:31:13,860 --> 00:31:19,540
from geography to history, chemistry, biology, run, run.

364
00:31:19,540 --> 00:31:24,100
And if I was one of the professors, teachers,

365
00:31:24,100 --> 00:31:30,300
I'd say, look, sit down, be quiet,

366
00:31:30,300 --> 00:31:34,700
for five minutes, be quiet.

367
00:31:34,700 --> 00:31:36,900
Look out of the window if you want to,

368
00:31:36,900 --> 00:31:40,900
see the beauty of light or the water or the leaf,

369
00:31:40,900 --> 00:31:44,340
look at this and that, but be quiet.

370
00:31:44,340 --> 00:31:47,180
A. We teach in classes that don't have windows now.

371
00:31:47,180 --> 00:31:48,980
K. Of course, naturally.

372
00:31:48,980 --> 00:31:51,260
A. Yes, I was just being... K. Of course, sir.

373
00:31:51,260 --> 00:31:53,820
A. But not only for station, it's a horror.

374
00:31:53,820 --> 00:31:55,460
K. Horror, that's all.

375
00:31:55,460 --> 00:31:58,940
You are trained to be functional. You follow, sir?

376
00:31:58,940 --> 00:32:02,340
A. I know.

377
00:32:02,340 --> 00:32:08,380
Don't look at anything else but be monkeys.

378
00:32:08,380 --> 00:32:11,380
And my child is brought up that way.

379
00:32:11,380 --> 00:32:14,220
A. Yes.

380
00:32:14,220 --> 00:32:17,220
K. I mean, it is appalling.

381
00:32:17,220 --> 00:32:20,900
A. The classroom is a tomb. Yes.

382
00:32:20,900 --> 00:32:25,460
K. So I say, sit quiet.

383
00:32:25,460 --> 00:32:29,700
Then after sitting quietly I talk about this first.

384
00:32:29,700 --> 00:32:31,740
I have done this in schools,

385
00:32:31,740 --> 00:32:36,340
talk about this, freedom, authority, beauty, love,

386
00:32:36,340 --> 00:32:38,740
you know, all that we have been discussing,

387
00:32:38,740 --> 00:32:41,820
then pick up your book.

388
00:32:41,820 --> 00:32:45,100
But you have learnt much more here than in the book.

389
00:32:45,100 --> 00:32:46,460
A. Oh, yes.

390
00:32:46,460 --> 00:32:49,180
K. Therefore the book shows what you are... you follow?

391
00:32:49,180 --> 00:32:53,020
A. Yes, exactly.

392
00:32:53,020 --> 00:32:55,140
The book is seen...

393
00:32:55,140 --> 00:32:57,300
K. The book becomes a second-hand thing.

394
00:32:57,300 --> 00:33:02,300
A. Yes, but seen with a clean eye.

395
00:33:04,500 --> 00:33:06,300
K. That's why, sir,

396
00:33:06,300 --> 00:33:11,700
I personally have never read a single book of all this,

397
00:33:11,700 --> 00:33:16,540
neither the Gita, the Upanishads, all that,

398
00:33:16,540 --> 00:33:19,340
what the Buddha has said, it somehow bored me.

399
00:33:19,340 --> 00:33:24,100
Sorry, it meant nothing to me.

400
00:33:24,100 --> 00:33:28,380
What has meant anything was to observe,

401
00:33:30,140 --> 00:33:34,500
observe the very poor in India,

402
00:33:35,460 --> 00:33:38,220
observe the rich,

403
00:33:38,220 --> 00:33:41,300
the dictators, the Mussolinis, the Hitlers,

404
00:33:41,300 --> 00:33:44,620
the Khrushchevs and Brezhnev,

405
00:33:44,620 --> 00:33:48,140
all watch them, in a politician,

406
00:33:48,140 --> 00:33:50,940
and you learn an awful lot,

407
00:33:50,940 --> 00:33:55,820
because the real book is you.

408
00:33:55,820 --> 00:33:56,860
You understand, sir?

409
00:33:56,860 --> 00:34:00,060
If you can read your book, which is yourself,

410
00:34:00,060 --> 00:34:02,700
you have learnt everything,

411
00:34:02,700 --> 00:34:06,620
except the functional knowledge.

412
00:34:06,620 --> 00:34:12,620
So, when there is self-knowing,

413
00:34:12,620 --> 00:34:16,940
authority has no meaning.

414
00:34:16,940 --> 00:34:18,860
I won't accept.

415
00:34:18,860 --> 00:34:21,980
Why should I accept these people

416
00:34:21,980 --> 00:34:25,860
that bring truth from India?

417
00:34:27,580 --> 00:34:32,940
That's not truth, they are bringing a tradition,

418
00:34:33,780 --> 00:34:36,980
what they believe.

419
00:34:38,700 --> 00:34:43,420
So, can the mind

420
00:34:44,140 --> 00:34:48,660
put away everything that man has talked

421
00:34:48,660 --> 00:34:52,260
or invented, imagined

422
00:34:52,260 --> 00:34:57,380
about religion, God, this and that?

423
00:34:57,380 --> 00:35:00,340
That means, can this mind,

424
00:35:00,340 --> 00:35:01,820
which is the mind of the world,

425
00:35:01,820 --> 00:35:07,900
which is the mind of common consciousness,

426
00:35:07,900 --> 00:35:11,620
can that consciousness empty itself

427
00:35:11,620 --> 00:35:17,380
of all the things man has said about reality?

428
00:35:19,660 --> 00:35:21,900
Otherwise, I can't... You follow, sir?

429
00:35:21,900 --> 00:35:24,340
A. Can't begin. K. Not only begin.

430
00:35:24,340 --> 00:35:27,700
What do I discover? What other people have said?

431
00:35:27,700 --> 00:35:33,300
What Buddha, Christ, why should I accept them?

432
00:35:33,300 --> 00:35:36,220
A. Well, the terrible thing is, I'm not in a position

433
00:35:36,220 --> 00:35:40,300
to grasp whatever they said that was worthwhile,

434
00:35:40,300 --> 00:35:45,740
until this occurs.

435
00:35:45,740 --> 00:35:47,820
This is...

436
00:35:47,820 --> 00:35:52,220
So, freedom, sir, is absolutely necessary.

437
00:35:52,220 --> 00:35:53,740
A. Oh yes, absolutely.

438
00:35:53,740 --> 00:35:57,500
K. But none of them say this.

439
00:35:58,580 --> 00:36:01,700
On the contrary, they say,

440
00:36:01,700 --> 00:36:04,420
freedom will come to you much later.

441
00:36:04,420 --> 00:36:07,340
Be in the prison for the rest of your life,

442
00:36:07,340 --> 00:36:10,580
when you die you will have freedom.

443
00:36:10,580 --> 00:36:14,820
That's what they are preaching, essentially.

444
00:36:14,820 --> 00:36:22,780
So, can the mind, the heart,

445
00:36:22,780 --> 00:36:26,980
and all the storehouse in the brain

446
00:36:26,980 --> 00:36:34,500
be free of the things that man has said about reality?

447
00:36:34,500 --> 00:36:37,380
Sir, that's a marvellous question. You understand, sir?

448
00:36:37,380 --> 00:36:39,540
A. Oh, I do, I do.

449
00:36:39,540 --> 00:36:43,460
One of the things that seems to me

450
00:36:43,460 --> 00:36:47,620
of remarkable cogency in our discussions,

451
00:36:47,620 --> 00:36:52,500
in our conversations, has been

452
00:36:52,500 --> 00:36:57,860
how continually you've returned to a question.

453
00:36:57,860 --> 00:36:58,900
K. Yes.

454
00:36:58,900 --> 00:37:01,620
A. Return to the question,

455
00:37:01,620 --> 00:37:08,660
and the notion of return in its depth,

456
00:37:08,660 --> 00:37:16,260
has, it seems, if I followed you correctly,

457
00:37:16,260 --> 00:37:24,420
been quite erroneously presented,

458
00:37:24,420 --> 00:37:29,140
the return has been presented as a movement to an answer.

459
00:37:29,140 --> 00:37:30,700
K. Quite, quite.

460
00:37:30,700 --> 00:37:32,820
A. But that is not a return.

461
00:37:32,820 --> 00:37:34,100
K. Of course not.

462
00:37:34,100 --> 00:37:39,620
Because the turn is towards that original that you mentioned.

463
00:37:39,620 --> 00:37:47,140
Therefore, it is to the question, not to the answer, at all.

464
00:37:47,140 --> 00:37:50,660
K. Quite, quite right. Quite right, sir.

465
00:37:50,660 --> 00:37:53,860
You know, I was staying once in Kashmir,

466
00:37:53,860 --> 00:37:57,940
right among the mountains,

467
00:37:57,940 --> 00:38:03,260
and a group of monks came to see me,

468
00:38:03,260 --> 00:38:05,460
freshly bathed and everything,

469
00:38:05,460 --> 00:38:07,700
done all the ceremony and all that,

470
00:38:07,700 --> 00:38:09,180
had come to see me.

471
00:38:09,180 --> 00:38:12,380
And they told me, they said they had just come

472
00:38:12,380 --> 00:38:21,020
from a group of unworldly people, who were super monks,

473
00:38:21,020 --> 00:38:25,060
who were very high up in the mountains.

474
00:38:25,060 --> 00:38:29,100
And I said, they are totally unworldly.

475
00:38:29,100 --> 00:38:32,140
I said, what do you mean by that word, sirs?

476
00:38:32,140 --> 00:38:35,060
They said they have just left the world,

477
00:38:35,060 --> 00:38:38,620
they are no longer tempted by the world.

478
00:38:38,620 --> 00:38:44,860
And they have this great knowledge of the world.

479
00:38:44,860 --> 00:38:48,380
And I said, when they have left the world,

480
00:38:48,380 --> 00:38:55,100
have they left the memory of the world?

481
00:38:55,100 --> 00:39:01,580
The memory, the knowledge which the world has made?

482
00:39:01,580 --> 00:39:03,940
You follow?

483
00:39:03,940 --> 00:39:06,700
Which the gurus have put together, the teachers.

484
00:39:06,700 --> 00:39:10,860
He said, that's wisdom.

485
00:39:10,860 --> 00:39:12,660
How can you leave wisdom?

486
00:39:12,660 --> 00:39:16,180
I said, do you mean wisdom is bought through a book,

487
00:39:16,180 --> 00:39:19,180
through a teacher, from another,

488
00:39:19,180 --> 00:39:24,140
through sacrifice, torture, renunciation?

489
00:39:24,140 --> 00:39:25,820
You follow, sir, their idea?

490
00:39:25,820 --> 00:39:36,780
That is, wisdom is something you can buy from somebody else.

491
00:39:36,780 --> 00:39:40,380
A. They went up the mountain with all this baggage.

492
00:39:40,380 --> 00:39:43,620
K. Baggage, that's right. That's exactly what I said.

493
00:39:43,620 --> 00:39:46,860
All the baggage which you have put away,

494
00:39:46,860 --> 00:39:51,820
the world you have put away, but you carry their baggage.

495
00:39:51,820 --> 00:39:52,820
You follow, sir?

496
00:39:52,820 --> 00:39:55,420
Good, actually.

497
00:39:56,940 --> 00:40:00,140
So that is a really important thing,

498
00:40:00,140 --> 00:40:04,860
if a mind is really very serious,

499
00:40:05,700 --> 00:40:10,020
to find out what religion means.

500
00:40:10,940 --> 00:40:14,980
Not all this rubbish.

501
00:40:14,980 --> 00:40:18,420
I keep on repeating because that seems to be mounting,

502
00:40:18,420 --> 00:40:21,460
you know, growing.

503
00:40:22,460 --> 00:40:27,740
But to free the mind from all the growth, the accretions,

504
00:40:29,020 --> 00:40:33,220
and therefore which means, see the accretions,

505
00:40:33,220 --> 00:40:37,260
see all the absurdities.

506
00:40:38,020 --> 00:40:41,660
A. It throws a very, very different cast on our word, worldly.

507
00:40:41,660 --> 00:40:44,020
K. Yes, that's just it.

508
00:40:44,020 --> 00:40:49,100
A. They are going up the mountain in order to leave the world,

509
00:40:49,100 --> 00:40:52,740
but they are taking immense pains to take it with them.

510
00:40:52,740 --> 00:40:53,740
K. That's right, sir.

511
00:40:53,740 --> 00:40:56,020
That's what they are doing when they go into the monastery.

512
00:40:56,020 --> 00:40:59,580
A. Of course, of course, of course, of course.

513
00:40:59,580 --> 00:41:02,180
Goodness!

514
00:41:02,500 --> 00:41:05,420
Accretions and crustaceans.

515
00:41:05,420 --> 00:41:07,220
K. So can I come back?

516
00:41:07,220 --> 00:41:12,980
Can the mind be completely alone,

517
00:41:13,260 --> 00:41:17,620
not isolated, not withdrawn,

518
00:41:17,620 --> 00:41:22,940
not build a wall round itself, say, and then I am alone,

519
00:41:22,940 --> 00:41:27,420
but alone in the sense

520
00:41:27,420 --> 00:41:32,900
that aloneness that comes when you put away all this,

521
00:41:33,900 --> 00:41:38,020
all the things of thought.

522
00:41:38,020 --> 00:41:39,660
You understand, sir?

523
00:41:39,660 --> 00:41:45,700
Because thought is so clever, cunning,

524
00:41:45,700 --> 00:41:50,740
it can build a marvellous structure

525
00:41:50,740 --> 00:41:54,780
and call that reality.

526
00:41:54,780 --> 00:41:59,060
But thought is the response of the past.

527
00:41:59,060 --> 00:42:01,460
So it is of time.

528
00:42:01,460 --> 00:42:09,860
Thought being of time cannot create something which has no time.

529
00:42:09,860 --> 00:42:13,260
Thought can function in that field of knowledge,

530
00:42:13,260 --> 00:42:17,540
it is necessary, but not in the other.

531
00:42:19,100 --> 00:42:24,620
And this doesn't need bravery,

532
00:42:24,620 --> 00:42:29,500
it doesn't need sacrifice, it doesn't need torture,

533
00:42:29,500 --> 00:42:34,300
just perception of the false.

534
00:42:34,300 --> 00:42:40,380
To see the false is to see the truth in the false.

535
00:42:40,380 --> 00:42:41,380
I don't know if you...

536
00:42:41,380 --> 00:42:45,980
A. To see the false is to see the truth in the false.

537
00:42:45,980 --> 00:42:47,420
I must repeat that again.

538
00:42:47,420 --> 00:42:55,380
To see the false is to see the truth in the false.

539
00:42:55,380 --> 00:43:03,860
K. And see what is considered truth as the false.

540
00:43:03,860 --> 00:43:08,460
A. Yes.

541
00:43:08,460 --> 00:43:13,300
So, my eyes are stripped of all the false,

542
00:43:15,140 --> 00:43:22,100
so that there is no inward deception whatsoever.

543
00:43:22,100 --> 00:43:26,580
Because there is no desire to see something,

544
00:43:26,580 --> 00:43:30,780
to achieve something.

545
00:43:30,780 --> 00:43:35,020
Because the moment there is a desire to experience,

546
00:43:35,020 --> 00:43:40,420
to achieve, to arrive at enlightenment, all that,

547
00:43:40,420 --> 00:43:44,980
there is going to be illusion.

548
00:43:44,980 --> 00:43:51,020
Something desire has created.

549
00:43:51,020 --> 00:43:57,580
Therefore, the mind must be free of this pursuit of desire

550
00:43:57,580 --> 00:44:03,140
and its fulfilment, which we discussed previously.

551
00:44:03,140 --> 00:44:07,420
Understand what the structure of desire is.

552
00:44:07,420 --> 00:44:10,620
We went and talked about it, a great deal about that.

553
00:44:10,620 --> 00:44:18,580
So, it comes to this point, can the mind be free,

554
00:44:19,580 --> 00:44:22,620
and free of all the things

555
00:44:22,620 --> 00:44:28,140
which are born of fear and desire and pleasure?

556
00:44:29,140 --> 00:44:37,580
That means one has to understand oneself at great depth.

557
00:44:38,580 --> 00:44:46,580
A. The thing that keeps popping up is

558
00:44:46,580 --> 00:44:50,980
that one can repeat those questions

559
00:44:50,980 --> 00:44:57,420
and start to think

560
00:44:57,420 --> 00:45:00,820
that he has grasped them.

561
00:45:00,820 --> 00:45:05,020
K. You grasp the words. A. Exactly.

562
00:45:05,020 --> 00:45:08,140
There is something that you have to come out the other side of.

563
00:45:08,140 --> 00:45:11,180
K. Quite right.

564
00:45:11,180 --> 00:45:16,580
A. But the repetition of the question

565
00:45:16,580 --> 00:45:23,100
does have a functional value, it seems to me.

566
00:45:23,100 --> 00:45:25,660
K. Yes, sir, it does.

567
00:45:25,660 --> 00:45:27,900
That is, if the person is willing to listen.

568
00:45:27,900 --> 00:45:30,860
A. If he is willing to listen.

569
00:45:30,860 --> 00:45:35,300
Because thought is incredibly deceitful,

570
00:45:35,300 --> 00:45:39,260
as you pointed out.

571
00:45:45,980 --> 00:45:52,500
Goodness, I was just thinking of poor old Jeremiah's words,

572
00:45:52,500 --> 00:45:59,180
the heart is desperately wicked and deceitful above all things.

573
00:45:59,180 --> 00:46:02,380
Surely he must have... K. ...tasted something.

574
00:46:02,380 --> 00:46:07,540
A. Yes, and of course, as with the whole line, we did them in.

575
00:46:07,540 --> 00:46:10,780
But I was asking myself this question

576
00:46:10,780 --> 00:46:21,260
concerning why I went on to continue my formal education.

577
00:46:21,300 --> 00:46:25,540
And in following this deeply, it seems to me to go back to something

578
00:46:25,540 --> 00:46:28,700
that is going to sound very absurd.

579
00:46:28,700 --> 00:46:35,660
But it has something to do with everything you've been talking about.

580
00:46:35,660 --> 00:46:40,060
When I was very small, growing up in England,

581
00:46:40,060 --> 00:46:42,260
I was put to school rather earlier

582
00:46:42,260 --> 00:46:45,100
than many American children put to school,

583
00:46:45,100 --> 00:46:51,700
and I always read a great deal of poetry.

584
00:46:53,540 --> 00:46:55,340
I don't know what's happened to us in this country,

585
00:46:55,340 --> 00:47:00,180
but poetry doesn't really exist for the populace at all.

586
00:47:00,180 --> 00:47:07,940
But thank God, I was brought up on it daily.

587
00:47:07,940 --> 00:47:11,460
K. Yes, in England, of course, everyone reads poetry,

588
00:47:11,460 --> 00:47:13,860
Greek, Latin, we all went through.

589
00:47:13,860 --> 00:47:21,420
And I always read poetry by the young woman employed by my parents

590
00:47:21,420 --> 00:47:26,420
to look after me and my little sister, and so forth.

591
00:47:26,420 --> 00:47:28,420
I never went to sleep without hearing it.

592
00:47:28,420 --> 00:47:31,780
One day, when I was very small, at school,

593
00:47:31,780 --> 00:47:32,980
the teacher read,

594
00:47:32,980 --> 00:47:37,340
the owl and the pussycat went to sea in a beautiful pea-green boat.

595
00:47:37,340 --> 00:47:42,220
That mad thing, marvellously mad thing, Edward Lear wrote.

596
00:47:42,220 --> 00:47:44,260
K. Edward Lear, yes.

597
00:47:44,260 --> 00:47:50,260
And you know, I was never the same again.

598
00:47:50,260 --> 00:47:54,180
And I know now why this sounds absolutely absurd.

599
00:47:54,180 --> 00:47:58,980
I came to experience in language a splendour

600
00:47:58,980 --> 00:48:03,860
that I never lost touch with,

601
00:48:03,860 --> 00:48:08,300
despite all the struggles I had with my teachers.

602
00:48:08,340 --> 00:48:10,780
I had a bad time in school,

603
00:48:10,780 --> 00:48:13,380
to get to the end of formal education

604
00:48:13,380 --> 00:48:15,700
and have to say that doesn't sound very good, but I did.

605
00:48:15,700 --> 00:48:18,540
I had a pretty grim time.

606
00:48:18,540 --> 00:48:20,140
One of the reasons for the grim time

607
00:48:20,140 --> 00:48:22,700
was my refusal to give this up.

608
00:48:22,700 --> 00:48:25,100
K. The pussycat in the boat.

609
00:48:25,100 --> 00:48:30,260
A. The fact that there's a bird and a cat in the same boat.

610
00:48:30,260 --> 00:48:33,580
The man is describing what you've called act, movement,

611
00:48:33,580 --> 00:48:36,300
in which truth and beauty and so on

612
00:48:36,300 --> 00:48:40,980
move along. Oh, goodness!

613
00:48:43,900 --> 00:48:48,860
K. I think we ought to, after coming to this point,

614
00:48:49,820 --> 00:48:53,260
we ought to go very deeply again.

615
00:48:53,260 --> 00:48:57,060
It's a question of meditation. A. Yes.

616
00:48:57,060 --> 00:49:02,460
K. Because religion, in the sense we are talking about,

617
00:49:02,460 --> 00:49:05,980
and meditation go together.

618
00:49:07,300 --> 00:49:11,140
That means religion isn't just an idea,

619
00:49:11,140 --> 00:49:16,300
but it's actual conduct in daily life.

620
00:49:21,340 --> 00:49:28,340
Your thoughts, your speech, your behaviour

621
00:49:28,340 --> 00:49:32,060
is the very essence of religion.

622
00:49:32,060 --> 00:49:33,860
You understand, sir?

623
00:49:33,860 --> 00:49:37,780
If that doesn't exist, religion can't exist.

624
00:49:37,780 --> 00:49:39,380
A. Exactly. K. It's just words.

625
00:49:39,380 --> 00:49:41,540
You can go on, spinning a lot of words,

626
00:49:41,540 --> 00:49:45,340
go to various circus tents, but that's not religion.

627
00:49:45,340 --> 00:49:50,140
So, establishing that deeply in oneself

628
00:49:50,140 --> 00:49:52,140
and the understanding of religion,

629
00:49:52,140 --> 00:50:00,380
in which then the next thing is, what is meditation?

630
00:50:00,380 --> 00:50:05,220
Because that is of tremendous importance,

631
00:50:05,220 --> 00:50:10,740
because meditation is something that really,

632
00:50:10,740 --> 00:50:12,980
if it is understood properly,

633
00:50:12,980 --> 00:50:19,180
is the most extraordinary thing the man can have.

634
00:50:19,180 --> 00:50:24,220
Meditation is not divorced from daily life.

635
00:50:24,220 --> 00:50:28,620
A. What was running through my mind was the

636
00:50:28,620 --> 00:50:34,740
– not mistaken – the root relation to the word

637
00:50:34,740 --> 00:50:36,780
medisthai, medeo.

638
00:50:36,780 --> 00:50:42,860
K. Medeo is to think, to ponder, to go into.

639
00:50:42,860 --> 00:50:48,140
A. In Homer it actually carries the idea of to provide for

640
00:50:48,140 --> 00:50:50,540
in the sense of to care for.

641
00:50:50,540 --> 00:50:53,140
Very beautiful.

642
00:50:53,140 --> 00:50:56,260
It brings up the question that you raised earlier,

643
00:50:56,260 --> 00:51:01,380
of true care.

644
00:51:01,380 --> 00:51:05,580
K. Yes, sir.

645
00:51:05,580 --> 00:51:09,020
A. That one is not meditating unless he is

646
00:51:09,020 --> 00:51:09,900
K. Careful.

647
00:51:09,900 --> 00:51:12,500
A. Careful and caring.

648
00:51:12,500 --> 00:51:14,860
K. Caring more than careful.

649
00:51:14,860 --> 00:51:17,260
A. Yes.

650
00:51:17,260 --> 00:51:21,500
It's all there in the word, if we don't look.

651
00:51:21,500 --> 00:51:24,420
Won't have a look. Yes.

652
00:51:24,420 --> 00:51:27,860
Yes, please go on, please.

653
00:51:29,140 --> 00:51:35,860
K. You see, when we have divorced conduct from religion,

654
00:51:35,860 --> 00:51:38,900
which we have,

655
00:51:38,900 --> 00:51:43,820
divorced relationship from religion, which we have,

656
00:51:43,820 --> 00:51:48,500
divorced death from religion, which we have,

657
00:51:48,540 --> 00:51:55,300
divorced love from religion,

658
00:51:55,300 --> 00:52:00,420
because we have made love into something sensuous,

659
00:52:00,420 --> 00:52:04,900
something that is pleasurable,

660
00:52:04,900 --> 00:52:11,340
then religion, which is the factor of regeneration,

661
00:52:11,340 --> 00:52:14,620
disappears in man.

662
00:52:14,620 --> 00:52:18,900
And that's why we are so degenerate.

663
00:52:20,940 --> 00:52:25,100
And it is, if I may be very...

664
00:52:25,100 --> 00:52:30,100
unless you have this quality of a mind that is really religious,

665
00:52:30,100 --> 00:52:34,380
degeneracy is inevitable.

666
00:52:34,780 --> 00:52:35,860
You follow, sir?

667
00:52:35,860 --> 00:52:39,580
Look at the politicians who are supposed to be the rulers,

668
00:52:39,580 --> 00:52:42,380
the guides, the helpers of people,

669
00:52:43,300 --> 00:52:48,100
you see what is happening in this country and everywhere.

670
00:52:48,100 --> 00:52:52,860
They are so corrupt and they want to bring order.

671
00:52:52,860 --> 00:52:55,100
They are so irreligious.

672
00:52:55,100 --> 00:52:58,220
They may go to church and baptisteries, or whatever they are,

673
00:52:58,220 --> 00:53:01,740
and yet they are really irreligious,

674
00:53:01,740 --> 00:53:05,940
because they don't behave.

675
00:53:06,700 --> 00:53:14,060
So, man is becoming more and more degenerate.

676
00:53:14,060 --> 00:53:17,300
You can see it, sir.

677
00:53:17,300 --> 00:53:21,220
Because religion is the factor

678
00:53:21,220 --> 00:53:26,620
that brings a new quality of energy.

679
00:53:27,460 --> 00:53:32,900
It's the same old energy, but it has become a new quality.

680
00:53:33,140 --> 00:53:37,380
Sir, the brain doesn't degenerate.

681
00:53:37,380 --> 00:53:40,900
As we get older, we tend to degenerate.

682
00:53:40,900 --> 00:53:45,060
But it doesn't, because the freedom

683
00:53:45,060 --> 00:53:54,020
from every kind of security of the me has no place.

684
00:53:54,020 --> 00:53:56,100
A. I noticed this in class yesterday,

685
00:53:56,100 --> 00:54:01,140
this business about energy that you were just talking about.

686
00:54:01,300 --> 00:54:07,380
There was a quickening that took place.

687
00:54:09,060 --> 00:54:11,620
There was, at the end of the class,

688
00:54:11,620 --> 00:54:18,180
and it was strenuous, because of this terrible hesitation.

689
00:54:18,180 --> 00:54:25,380
But even so, there was a release of energy,

690
00:54:25,380 --> 00:54:30,820
which has nothing to do with entertainment.

691
00:54:31,460 --> 00:54:36,420
People are running to get their minds off themselves,

692
00:54:36,420 --> 00:54:40,340
which of course is nonsense.

693
00:54:40,340 --> 00:54:43,380
They're just grinding themselves into themselves some more with it.

694
00:54:43,380 --> 00:54:45,380
But in this particular case,

695
00:54:45,380 --> 00:54:48,340
there was empirical demonstration of what you're saying.

696
00:54:48,340 --> 00:54:51,140
Something that is out there, it's to be seen, it's observable.

697
00:54:51,140 --> 00:54:57,940
And behold, it sprung up like a green bay tree.

698
00:54:57,940 --> 00:55:01,620
Yes, please, go on.

699
00:55:01,620 --> 00:55:06,740
You see, sir, that's why the priests throughout the world

700
00:55:06,740 --> 00:55:11,860
have made religion into something profitable,

701
00:55:11,860 --> 00:55:16,660
both the worshipper and the intermediary.

702
00:55:16,660 --> 00:55:20,820
It has become a business affair,

703
00:55:20,820 --> 00:55:23,860
intellectually a business,

704
00:55:23,860 --> 00:55:27,540
or it has become really commercial,

705
00:55:27,540 --> 00:55:32,420
not only physically, but inwardly, deeply.

706
00:55:32,420 --> 00:55:36,260
Do this and you will reach that.

707
00:55:36,260 --> 00:55:38,020
A.S. – utilitarian to the core.

708
00:55:38,020 --> 00:55:41,780
K. – which is commercial.

709
00:55:43,860 --> 00:55:48,340
And so, unless this is put an end to,

710
00:55:48,340 --> 00:55:52,900
we are going to degenerate more and more and more.

711
00:55:52,900 --> 00:55:59,220
And that's why I feel so immensely responsible,

712
00:55:59,220 --> 00:56:03,300
personally, tremendously responsible,

713
00:56:03,300 --> 00:56:06,820
to the audience when I talk,

714
00:56:06,820 --> 00:56:09,460
when I go to the various schools in India,

715
00:56:09,460 --> 00:56:12,180
I feel I am responsible for those children.

716
00:56:12,180 --> 00:56:13,220
You follow, sir?

717
00:56:13,220 --> 00:56:15,940
A.S. – yes, of course, I do. I certainly do.

718
00:56:15,940 --> 00:56:18,500
K. – I say, for God's sake, be different,

719
00:56:18,500 --> 00:56:22,340
don't grow up like that.

720
00:56:22,340 --> 00:56:26,020
I go into very, very, you know, talk a great deal,

721
00:56:26,020 --> 00:56:31,140
and they begin to see, but the world is too strong for them.

722
00:56:31,140 --> 00:56:33,540
They have to earn a livelihood,

723
00:56:33,540 --> 00:56:35,140
they have to resist their parents

724
00:56:35,140 --> 00:56:38,100
who want them to settle down and have a good job,

725
00:56:38,100 --> 00:56:42,020
marry, a house, you know, all that business.

726
00:56:42,020 --> 00:56:46,580
And the public opinion, this overpopulation,

727
00:56:46,580 --> 00:56:50,340
is much too strong.

728
00:56:50,340 --> 00:56:52,660
A.S. – the tremendous weight of that tradition

729
00:56:52,660 --> 00:56:55,460
of the four stages of life.

730
00:56:55,460 --> 00:56:57,700
Of course. K. – So I say,

731
00:56:57,700 --> 00:57:01,140
let us find out, with our few elite

732
00:57:01,140 --> 00:57:02,980
– quote the word elite,

733
00:57:02,980 --> 00:57:06,740
if I may use that word without any snobbery –

734
00:57:06,740 --> 00:57:10,500
let's create a few.

735
00:57:10,500 --> 00:57:13,540
Really our concern,

736
00:57:13,540 --> 00:57:17,140
few teachers, few students.

737
00:57:17,140 --> 00:57:18,580
Even that becomes very difficult,

738
00:57:18,580 --> 00:57:24,660
because most teachers,

739
00:57:24,660 --> 00:57:26,260
they are not good at this or that,

740
00:57:26,260 --> 00:57:29,780
and therefore become teachers.

741
00:57:29,780 --> 00:57:32,180
And you know what they are.

742
00:57:32,180 --> 00:57:36,180
A.S. – Oh, yes. Oh dear, dear, dear, yes.

743
00:57:41,620 --> 00:57:48,180
K. – So everything, sir, is against you.

744
00:57:48,180 --> 00:57:49,700
Everything.

745
00:57:49,700 --> 00:57:52,900
The gurus are against you,

746
00:57:52,900 --> 00:57:56,260
the priests are against you,

747
00:57:56,260 --> 00:58:00,180
business people, the teachers, the politicians,

748
00:58:00,180 --> 00:58:02,740
everybody is against you.

749
00:58:02,740 --> 00:58:07,380
Take that for granted.

750
00:58:07,380 --> 00:58:09,540
They won't help you an inch.

751
00:58:09,540 --> 00:58:12,980
They want you to go their way.

752
00:58:12,980 --> 00:58:17,380
They have got their vested interests in all that.

753
00:58:17,380 --> 00:58:23,060
A.S. – Yes, I do see that with clarity.

754
00:58:23,060 --> 00:58:26,100
In our next conversation,

755
00:58:26,100 --> 00:58:28,340
do you think we could explore

756
00:58:28,340 --> 00:58:30,740
the activity of meditation

